{number: 104}
{title: My Jesus, I Love Thee}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [F] Jesus, I [Bb] love Thee, I [F] know Thou art [C7] mine;
For [F] Thee all the [Bb] follies of [F] sin I re-[C7] [F] sign;
My [F] gracious Re-[Bb] deemer, my [F] Savior art [C7] Thou;
If [F] ever I [Bb] loved Thee, my [F] Jesus, [C7] 'tis [F] now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I [F] love Thee be-[Bb] cause Thou hast [F] first loved [C7] me,
And [F] purchased my [Bb] pardon on [F] Calvary's [C7] [F] tree;
I [F] love Thee for [Bb] wearing the [F] thorns on Thy [C7] brow;
If [F] ever I [Bb] loved Thee, my [F] Jesus, [C7] 'tis [F] now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I'll [F] love Thee in [Bb] life, I will [F] love Thee in [C7] death,
And [F] praise Thee as [Bb] long as Thou [F] lendest me [C7] [F] breath;
And [F] say when the [Bb] death dew lies [F] cold on my [C7] brow,
If [F] ever I [Bb] loved Thee, my [F] Jesus, [C7] 'tis [F] now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
In [F] mansions of [Bb] glory and [F] endless de-[C7] light,
I'll [F] ever a-[Bb] dore Thee in [F] heaven so [C7] [F] bright;
I'll [F] sing with the [Bb] glittering [F] crown on my [C7] brow,
If [F] ever I [Bb] loved Thee, my [F] Jesus, [C7] 'tis [F] now.
{end_of_verse}
